bitUtils 0.2.1

- Loaders accept file or directory paths, so the same functions work in scripts
  and tests as well as with Tcl/Tk dialogs.
- Loaded tables are returned invisibly in addition to the usual assignment.
- Object names are sanitized with make.names(), including spaces in file names.
- New bit_read() dispatches to bit_csv() or bit_txt() by file extension.
- bit_cp949() converts a data frame or object name without a GUI; the chooser
  remains available when x is omitted.
- bit_setwd() accepts a directory path.
- bit_csv_all() and bit_txt_all() no longer block on a message box or sleep;
  set notify = TRUE to restore a completion dialog.
- bit_editor() evaluates in the global environment, resizes with the window,
  and adds Ctrl+O / Ctrl+S / Ctrl+R plus basic keyword highlighting.
- DESCRIPTION uses Authors@R, a GitHub URL, and testthat in Suggests.
- gWidgets2 is now suggested rather than imported, so CSV/TXT loading no
  longer depends on it.

bitUtils 0.1.2

- Added bit_editor() function, a Tcl/Tk text editor with scripting capabilities, load/save functionality, and a scrollbar.

bitUtils 0.1.1

- The bit_cp949() function has been added for the users of the Korean-language version of MS-Windows.

bitUtils 0.1

- Created bit_csv() and bit_txt() functions.
